[An editorial note: I tried to post this on Friday, but the newsprogram bitched
(no space (newslib) [innwatch:36] 74439 lt 7500). So the day when the ascension
took place was Thursday]

Haha! Hahah! Finally made it! YESSSS! I have been playing 3.1 since last 
November (that's when I finally got an UNIX account with NH3.1 - I also got
extra RAM for my PC as a christmas present and since then I have also been able
to play it on a PC since then) and now, yesterday, I finally MADE IT! Yes,
I have been reading this newsgroup all the time with actually ascending until
then :-) I never ascended in NH3.0 but I played it only for a couple of months
anyway.

This was the third really great character I ever had in NH3.1. The two others
were on UNIX, this one was on PC. The first great character was a barbarian
who found a WoW on dungeon level 1, but died because his save file became out-
of-date when those stupid sysadmins re-installed the program instead of making
an update. The next one was a samurai who got the amulet and was on his way
back, only 6 levels to the endgame... when his pet gelatinous cube ate his 
bag of holding (which had all the back-up weapons) and then Wiz stole the
Tsurugi. I still have the game but it is too boring to go on. (There is a
horde of monsters and double trouble waiting for me :-(  ) Will I get more
points if I quit?

Then... this absolutely awesome Caveman (yes, I really made my first ascension
with a CAVEMAN!!!) ascends! The same pal who asked how to make cursed potions
of water without pissing out your god a couple of days ago. Eventually I used
one wish from the WoW you get in the castle (the only WoW I ever found...),
only to meet two ghosts in the valley of death, both of whom had a potion of
unholy water. The only wish I had before that was (GDSM) from a fountain on
level 1. Some of you will probably not consider this sport, but I always drink
from fountains with level 1 characters. After all, you have nothing to lose
YET.

I got a SoR, GoP and the Vorpal Blade from the bones file of a barbarian.
I accidentally evaporated the Vorpal Blade, trying to enchant it to +7 (which
I thought was the safe limit) with uncursed enchant weapon. Then I was stuck
with a really miserable weapon (Liontamer... oh btw, this *is* nh313--, not the
standard version) until Anu finally dropped me Grayswandir. I also dipped and
got Excalibur (which was useful for dealing with Vlad...) 

Btw, when I still had the Vorpal Blade, I sometimes got the message
"Somehow, you swing wildly and miss!" 
It couldn't have been caused by monster invisibility, since I could see
invisible. Did it have something to do with my caveman's miserable dex?

I got speed boots, cloak of displacement and a helm of brilliance by polypiling
the stuff in Fort Ludios. I later drank an unidentified potion and it was 
polymorphing and I lost my cloak. In gehennom, I polypiled until I got a new
cloak of displacement. I didn't need a ring of conflict (every Caveman knows
why... :-)


Since I had never ascended before, I thought "well you can never be too sure"
and used the cursed bell until I had "most definitely enough hp". (Argh, how
I hate the gelatinous cube that ate 3 wraith corpses before I could kill it!!!
Next game I will probably genocide gelatinous cubes (if that's possible)).
I was lawful all the way through so I couldn't use the PYEC (don't know if
I would have even if I had been able... probably no). Since I am also 
practicing for the unix (I want to get on that damn scorelist!!!:-) I chose
not to use anything which I wouldn't be able to use on UNIX - this includes
making backups (besides, my 286 would be way too slow for them. Restoring a
game will take several minutes), bones cheating and other blatant cheats.

The endgame was much easier than what I had expected. By casting a worn-out
spell to get confused & reading gold detection you could find most portals 
quickly and with levitation/digging just run for them. I went through the
elemental planes so quickly that I met the Wiz only twice during the endgame.
He never appeared on the astral plane. 
Yes, I had been totally spoiled by reading other people's ascension posts and
such, so I made sure I turned the conflict (from the staff of might) OFF before
entering the Astral plane :-)
There I met mr. Pestilence whom I hacked down with Grayswandir before he could
infect me. Then I was surrounded by angels/priests and busy hacking them until
Pestilence got up again. Again, down he went before he had time infect me. 
Before he could get up again, I made a run for the altar (I was very fast),
I didn't bother to fight any monsters anymore - I just ran past them and let
my pet angel deal with them and pestilence. The altar was Anu's, so I simply
blew my magic whistle and offered the amulet...

Here is the new demigod's final score: (not a screen dump or anything such
since I don't know how to do that on a pc)

Goodbye Siegfried the Demigod (yes, Siegfried was a "caveman" - see the opera
				if you don't believe me :-)
You and the Angel of Anu
Went to your reward with 464754 points,
	an uncursed amulet of life saving (being worn) (worth 150 zorkmids),
	5 uncursed rubies (worth 17500 zorkmids),
	3 uncursed amethyst stones (worth 1800 zorkmids),
	3 emerald stones (worth 7500 zorkmids),
	3 diamonds (worth 12000 zorkmids),
	a blessed amulet of life saving (worth 150 zorkmids),
